Author: Adrian <adrian@construkted.com>
Date:   Sat Oct 17 16:20:01 2026 -0400

    fix(transition): repoint managed service launchers
    
    An independent review found transition paths that leave a host in
    recovery_required, and the development host showed another layout.
    
    - The worker reloads the user manager before it adopts a unit. A
      replaced unit file reports NeedDaemonReload until the reload.
    - Preparation replaces the gateway unit only when the unit runs the
      managed runtime. A unit that runs ~/.local/bin/hermes keeps its
      definition. Preparation refuses a replacement that changes KillMode
      or WorkingDirectory, a symlinked unit, and a drop-in that runs the
      managed runtime.
    - The managed release can publish a forwarder at the launcher that a
      unit runs, such as a workspace checkout launcher. The transition now
      publishes a stock forwarder at each such launcher.
    - A unit generator failure reports its last stderr line.
    
    The review report is in docs/agents/2026-10-17-inplace-fixes-review/.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

